  { id: 'cc-14', questionText: "What ingredients & measurements go into the Cantarito ? Example: 1oz Herradura Blanco Tequila, 1oz Lime Juice, 1oz Simple Syrup", correctAnswer: "BATCHED / SHARED FORMAT (185oz, served tableside in a large clay cantarito with small cantaros cups): 1 bottle Cazadores Blanco Tequila, 14oz Orange Juice, 20oz Grapefruit Juice, 8oz Agave, 8oz Fresh Lime Juice, 4 teaspoons Salt, plus Tajín & Salt (two sprinkles each) — combined in a large container and stirred, then topped with 1 bottle Owens Rio Red Grapefruit Soda (or 2 'squirts' from the soda gun) to taste. Garnish: lime wheel, tajín/salt rim. GRADING: this is a BATCH recipe, not a single build — do NOT require exact batch ounces. Naming the correct COMPONENTS (Cazadores Blanco, orange juice, grapefruit juice, lime juice, agave, salt, Owens Rio Red grapefruit soda) earns full credit. Correct ounces are a bonus. Knowing it is batched and shared tableside is part of the answer; a single-serve build is incorrect.", points: 2 }
